<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcaea</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φωκαία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a maritime town of
				Ionia</i>, <i>a colony of the Athenians</i>, <i>whose inhabitants fled</i>, <i>to
				escape from Persian domination</i>, <i>and founded
				Massilia</i>, now <i>Fouges</i> or <i>Foggia</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 17,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 31, § 119</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 30, 32, §
			121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 31 sq.</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 10,
				16, 4</span></i>, and v. 2. Phocis, B.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcaeensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>Phocœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Graeci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 4, 5, § 35</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcaeenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the Phocœans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				21, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38,
				39, 12</span></i> Drak. ad loc.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4,
				4, § 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 43,
				3, 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phō-caei</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Phocœans</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
			19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod.
				16, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcăĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Phocœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murex,</span>”
				<i>which was taken near Phocœa</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>Massilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 4,
					52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phocaicae Emporiae,</span>”
				<i>a Spanish town founded by the Massilians</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					369</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcăis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			adj., <i>Phocœan;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> for <i>Massilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 301</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ballista,</span>”
				<i>constructed with great skill by the Massilians</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					1, 335</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phōcenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Phocœa</i>, <i>the
				Phocœans</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 37,
				1, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
